    "answer": "The `processOrder` function turns a cart into an order [2]. It validates the cart using `OrderRequestSchema` (Zod) before making any network calls [2]. If valid, it sends a `POST /orders` request with the user's bearer token [2]. On success, it empties the cart and returns the order ID and total [2]. If an error occurs, it maps API errors to user-facing reasons, such as 409 for out of stock and 402 for payment declined [2].",
